You can refactor that loop into a single list comprehension by
combining the conditional filter (`if x.active`) with the
expression (`x.name.upper()`) like so:

```python
out = [x.name.upper() for x in items if x.active]
```

This produces an identical list to the original loop. It's also
considered more idiomatic Python and is generally a few percent
faster because the list growth is handled by the runtime rather
than per-element `.append()` calls.
